                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2850353,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "The Founding Fathers of The United States were inspired by the philosophy. George Washington was introduced to Stoicism by his neighbors at age 17, and later put on a play based on the life of Cato to inspire his men. Thomas Jefferson kept a copy of Seneca beside his bed. Writers and artists have also been inspired by the Stoics. Eugene Delacroix, the renowned French Romantic artist known best for his painting Liberty Leading the People, was an ardent Stoic, referring to it as his consoling religion.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2850354,
